# OI Linux guest inittab.
#
# Two things are added to Alpine's default: a getty on the serial port, so that the boot log the
# application keeps (`logs\console.log`) shows a usable console and support can log in without a
# network, and the six virtual consoles are dropped because the virtual machine has no display.
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

# tty1 is used for the boot output of the kernel and OpenRC
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
ttyS0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 0 ttyS0 vt100

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
::restart:/sbin/init
